espects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"bundles_separable_slices","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion that exercises spawn_detached() at runtime — e.g. a test that spawns a child and asserts it runs with the caller-supplied cwd, env (including push.py's secret-stripping preserved), and successful rebar re-entry — so the behavioral cutover is proven, not just the source structure.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8125,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2 is 'A STATIC test (source scan over src/rebar)' — structure only","AC5 is 'CI's pytest invocation are green' — generic, not tied to the spawn path","Provenance: the fixed bug was 'a missing cwd= on the detached Popen' — a runtime property invisible to a source scan","E6(f): a detached OS-process spawn is a live boundary; green offline/static checks that bypass the actual spawn do not prove the behavior"],"finding":"No acceptance criterion exercises the consolidated spawn_detached() at runtime as it runs in production; AC2's static source scan only proves the signature lives in _proc.py, and AC5's pytest is a generic invocation not named to cover the detached-spawn path. The very defect motivating this refactor (missing cwd=, bug 3198) was a runtime failure that a static scan would not catch — so the cutover to the shared helper needs a behavioral proving command (a test that spawn_detached actually launches a child with the correct durable cwd, PYTHONPATH bootstrap, and caller-supplied env/detach flags).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6f9dc62c706b37c5","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC2, AC5)","norm_id":"nede9c51dad12ed29","priority":0.1375,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future edit to spawn_detached drops or mis-layers the PYTHONPATH bootstrap or durable cwd; the static scan still passes because the tokens are present, but detached children fail at runtime exactly as in bug 3198"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add: '[ ] A behavioral test spawns a detached child via spawn_detached() from a since-removed cwd and asserts the child starts with the explicit durable cwd, imports rebar via the PYTHONPATH bootstrap, and receives the caller-provided env unmodified except for the layered PYTHONPATH.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Correct AC-2's out-of-scope paths to the real prefix src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py and .../adapters/jira_family/wiki_re